    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7806289c6792feb5330d8205c94f04754c8d08e4b83ef11d7e5d6c50205d27da",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The three physical interfaces have different logical directions: the wave reconstruction derives prime-localized spikes only after assuming RH, van der Pol's apparatus samples a critical-line quotient and finds finitely many zeros there, while the billiard proposal encodes RH in an ideal asymptotic survival tail whose sufficiently slow decay is presented as a possible refutation route. Making zeta observable therefore does not by itself provide global zero-locus certification.",
