    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_80a21a3909abd2b894ff3f620a968c1be11205418fda8914faa7aeec01350a5c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Möbius walk motivates square-root-scale typical cancellation, but analytic zero exclusion requires quantified deterministic control: the strict Mertens bound was false despite extensive finite agreement, a separate probability/Fourier walk yields only strip-level localization while tolerating off-line zeros, and the weaker all-ε Mertens growth criterion remains the RH-equivalent statement.",
