    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8b7a7272d053db650b51f1934735f3c1fc38dc91101bcf89f668de71ec984f50",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the xp proposal, inverse-spectrum realization, and the Connes and Okubo constructions, matching a leading zero count or encoding known critical-line zeros preserves too little structure to supply the Hilbert–Pólya mechanism: the resulting realization may be continuous or integrable, nonunique, nonnormalizable, or unable to exclude off-line zeros.",
