    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9b8afeea028183334c229afb48ad733c480d027ce7595bc1101707abd30cefc5",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The section separates three gates in a statistical-mechanical route: unique factorization and logarithmic energies can produce a zeta partition sum, a Möbius map can convert critical-line localization into unit-circle localization, and a circle theorem can transfer that geometry only for a model satisfying its interaction and limit hypotheses; the cited Knauf system fails the last gate.",
